WEBVTT

00:00.931 --> 00:03.667 align:center line:79%
We are grateful
for this schedule adjustment,

00:03.667 --> 00:07.804 align:center line:79%
which gives us more chance to gather
and talk about the scriptures.

00:08.906 --> 00:12.743 align:center line:79%
One of the most powerful places
for gospel learning is the home.

00:13.944 --> 00:16.647 align:center line:79%
It is even more
important than our classrooms.

00:17.814 --> 00:20.717 align:center line:79%
This schedule adjustment is
a meaningful opportunity

00:20.884 --> 00:26.256 align:center line:79%
to strengthen gospel learning at home
and focus more fully on Jesus Christ.

00:27.591 --> 00:30.000 align:center line:79%
Come, Follow Me reminds us
that the purpose of gospel learning is

00:30.000 --> 00:32.563 align:center line:79%
Come, Follow Me reminds us
that the purpose of gospel learning is

00:32.629 --> 00:37.167 align:center line:79%
to deepen our conversion and help
us become more like the Savior.

00:38.602 --> 00:40.604 align:center line:81%
The new schedule is designed

00:40.671 --> 00:45.442 align:center line:79%
to support the daily home-centered
efforts already taking place.

00:46.810 --> 00:49.246 align:center line:81%
As we study the scriptures at home

00:49.313 --> 00:52.282 align:center line:79%
and talk about what
we're learning at church,

00:52.282 --> 00:56.386 align:center line:79%
the gospel becomes more
personal and part of everyday life.

00:57.688 --> 01:00.000 align:center line:79%
When learning begins in the home
and is strengthened at church,

01:00.000 --> 01:01.892 align:center line:79%
When learning begins in the home
and is strengthened at church,

01:02.492 --> 01:07.331 align:center line:79%
it blesses individuals,
families, and entire wards and branches.

01:08.732 --> 01:11.735 align:center line:79%
That's why our Sunday School
time matters so much.

01:12.970 --> 01:17.741 align:center line:79%
Now, watch as this teacher models
how we can focus on Jesus Christ

01:18.408 --> 01:20.644 align:center line:81%
and support gospel learning at home.

01:22.746 --> 01:25.949 align:center line:79%
A common misconception is that if
you are a teacher, you are the talker.

01:25.949 --> 01:27.017 align:center line:81%
You are all knowledgeable.

01:27.050 --> 01:28.485 align:center line:81%
Welcome to Sunday School today.

01:28.485 --> 01:30.000 align:center line:79%
I am so excited to hear what
you guys have learned from Come,

01:30.000 --> 01:31.321 align:center line:79%
I am so excited to hear what
you guys have learned from Come,

01:31.321 --> 01:33.190 align:center line:81%
Follow Me and from Isaiah.

01:38.028 --> 01:40.998 align:center line:79%
By a show of hands, who was able
to read from Isaiah this week?

01:41.665 --> 01:42.766 align:center line:81%
Awesome. That's great.

01:42.766 --> 01:45.502 align:center line:79%
Now, to help you remember what you
might have studied during the week,

01:45.502 --> 01:47.037 align:center line:81%
I've written up some of the doctrine,

01:47.037 --> 01:51.241 align:center line:79%
as well as this question: What did
you learn this week about the Savior?

01:51.241 --> 01:53.610 align:center line:79%
And I would love
to hear your thoughts on this.

01:53.610 --> 01:55.612 align:center line:79%
To help you remember what
you've learned and studied,

01:55.612 --> 01:58.181 align:center line:79%
I'm going to give you a couple seconds
to look back in your scriptures,

01:58.181 --> 02:00.000 align:center line:79%
look at any notes, and then I'm
gonna give you the opportunity to share

02:00.000 --> 02:00.484 align:center line:79%
look at any notes, and then I'm
gonna give you the opportunity to share

02:00.484 --> 02:01.952 align:center line:81%
with the person sitting next to you.

02:01.952 --> 02:04.287 align:center line:79%
So go ahead and take just a little
bit to remember what it is that you

02:04.287 --> 02:06.556 align:center line:81%
studied this week. In Come, Follow Me,

02:06.556 --> 02:08.725 align:center line:79%
it really encourages teachers
to be the facilitator,

02:08.725 --> 02:11.728 align:center line:79%
to create opportunities for people
to share what they are learning.

02:11.728 --> 02:13.964 align:center line:79%
I am a strong believer
that if I am the only one talking

02:13.964 --> 02:16.166 align:center line:79%
and sharing what I am learning
in the scriptures,

02:16.166 --> 02:19.603 align:center line:79%
the class is not nearly
as meaningful and rich as it could be.

02:19.603 --> 02:21.004 align:center line:81%
I always, in every class,

02:21.004 --> 02:22.072 align:center line:81%
try to invite class members

02:22.072 --> 02:24.141 align:center line:79%
to share what they are studying
and learning about Jesus Christ

02:24.141 --> 02:25.776 align:center line:79%
in their personal
and family scripture study.

02:26.209 --> 02:28.045 align:center line:81%
I heard some wonderful comments out there,

02:28.045 --> 02:30.000 align:center line:79%
and I would love to have you
share if you feel comfortable

02:30.000 --> 02:30.013 align:center line:79%
and I would love to have you
share if you feel comfortable

02:30.013 --> 02:32.916 align:center line:79%
with the class. Do we have anyone
that would like to start us off?

02:33.984 --> 02:36.887 align:center line:81%
President D. Todd Christofferson declared,

02:37.587 --> 02:42.426 align:center line:79%
"The central purpose of all
scripture is to fill our souls with faith

02:42.492 --> 02:45.762 align:center line:79%
in God the Father
and in His Son, Jesus Christ.

02:46.630 --> 02:52.703 align:center line:79%
The message and spiritual power
of the scriptures lead us to salvation.

02:52.769 --> 02:57.007 align:center line:79%
Our decision to read and study
the scriptures is an important

02:57.074 --> 03:00.000 align:center line:79%
step toward becoming like
Heavenly Father and Jesus Christ."

03:00.000 --> 03:01.311 align:center line:79%
step toward becoming like
Heavenly Father and Jesus Christ."

03:02.746 --> 03:05.515 align:center line:81%
The home is the center of gospel learning,

03:06.049 --> 03:10.120 align:center line:79%
and Sunday School is meant
to support what's happening there.

03:11.621 --> 03:15.192 align:center line:79%
Sunday School involves
discussion and learning from others.

03:16.393 --> 03:19.529 align:center line:79%
It is not just
a presentation by a teacher.

03:20.897 --> 03:24.234 align:center line:79%
Teachers don't need to cover
every part of the lesson.

03:25.102 --> 03:30.000 align:center line:79%
Instead, invite others to share
their thoughts and testimonies.

03:30.000 --> 03:30.307 align:center line:79%
Instead, invite others to share
their thoughts and testimonies.

03:31.608 --> 03:37.147 align:center line:79%
As we prepare each week by studying
the scriptures at home and using the Come,

03:37.247 --> 03:42.719 align:center line:79%
Follow Me resource, we can learn
with the Spirit guiding the conversation

03:42.819 --> 03:46.389 align:center line:79%
at church, helping us
learn from one another.

03:47.624 --> 03:49.893 align:center line:81%
Because class time is limited,

03:50.660 --> 03:56.032 align:center line:79%
it's important to begin promptly and focus
on the teachings, example,

03:57.000 --> 04:00.000 align:center line:81%
sacrifice, and love of Jesus Christ.

04:00.000 --> 04:00.504 align:center line:81%
sacrifice, and love of Jesus Christ.

04:01.404 --> 04:02.906 align:center line:81%
Every minute matters.
